 "result": "Call order (this repo is a Flask-like framework named `tessel`):\n\n1. `Tessel.__call__` — `src/tessel/app.py:1618`; just delegates to `wsgi_entry`.\n2. `Tessel.wsgi_entry` — `src/tessel/app.py:1566`; this is the real WSGI app, so middleware can wrap it.\n3. `Tessel.request_context` — `src/tessel/app.py:1501`; builds the context via `AppContext.from_environ`.\n4. `AppContext.push` — `src/tessel/ctx.py:416`:\n   - sets the context var and sends `appcontext_pushed`\n   - opens the session via `_get_session`\n   - calls `AppContext.match_request` (`src/tessel/ctx.py:405`), which does URL routing and stores `url_rule`/`view_args` or a `routing_exception`\n5. `Tessel.run_full_request` — `src/tessel/app.py:992`:\n   - sends the `request_started` signal\n   - calls `Tessel.preprocess_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:1366`), which runs `url_value_preprocessors` and then `before_request_funcs`; a non-None return short-circuits the view\n6. `Tessel.run_view` — `src/tessel/app.py:966`:\n   - raises the routing exception if matching failed\n   - answers OPTIONS automatically if applicable\n   - calls the view as `self.ensure_sync(self.view_functions[rule.endpoint])(**view_args)` (`src/tessel/app.py:990`)\n\nAfter the view returns, `finalize_request` and then `finalize_reply` (`src/tessel/app.py:1394`) run, and exceptions go through `route_user_fault` / `route_unhandled_fault`.",
